aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r1: argue/scope: A1: read with the necessity on its consequent alone, (known_us → □is) ∧ god_more_certain → (known_god → □is), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, (known_us → □is) ∧ god_more_certain → □(known_god → is), C1 (S2) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r1: argue/scope: P1 (S2): read with the necessity on its consequent alone, known_us → □is, the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □(known_us → is), C1 (S2) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
